{
  "id": "q-1191",
  "parts": [
    {
      "part": "problem",
      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "Find all of the subsets of $A=\\{x,y,z\\}.$",
      "original_html_sha256": "30cd9e73708a268810ee56666d9836cbeee7008930c691ae1060cf45c53c7a92",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/repairs/source-provenance-v2/structured-source/source/30cd9e73708a268810ee56666d9836cbeee7008930c691ae1060cf45c53c7a92.html",
      "extraction_errors": []
    },
    {
      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "To find every subset of $A,$ we list out every combination of elements within $A.$\n\nWe can use the following diagram to visualize the process:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/assets/1d7c11586a8fff5f63d46d936fd32c7b5fbfc33a406ddf268bfdd934fe787cdf.png)\n\nNote that we must include the empty set since it is a subset of every set.\n\nBy doing this, we get\n\n$$\n∅,\\{x\\},\\{y\\},\\{z\\},\\{x,y\\},\\{x,z\\},\\{y,z\\},\\{x,y,z\\}.\n$$",
      "original_html_sha256": "cbfab5985ca7afd9984692c323dd274bc5d7b165aac0e9ee1ff19d96c16d69a5",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/repairs/source-provenance-v2/structured-source/source/cbfab5985ca7afd9984692c323dd274bc5d7b165aac0e9ee1ff19d96c16d69a5.html",
      "extraction_errors": []
    }
  ]
}
